["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/plannedTransportRoutes", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A transport route refers to the planned path or network used to move people, goods, data, or resources from one location to another.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SoftwarePurpose/firmware", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The Element provides low level control over a device's hardware.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SoftwareArtifact", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibid", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Business Identifier (IBID)](https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/) is a verifiable unique identifier for legal entities as defined in the [ISO/DIS 25500-3](https://www.iso.org/standard/87705.html) draft standard. It is composed of three data elements: the International Business Registration Number (IBRN), the legal name, and the date of origin formatted as eight numeric characters (YYYYMMDD). Each element is separated by a pipe character (`|`) (e.g., `US-DE.BER:3031657|Code Management Association|19990420`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Build/parameter", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:N7cfc71cd06f74d8fa40f8d2ebcc4dff6", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#datatype", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Dataset/dataPreprocessing", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Preprocessing steps that were applied to the raw data to create the given dataset.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isan", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Audiovisual Number (ISAN)](https://www.isan.org/about/#what_is_isan) is a unique 24-digit hexadecimal identifier for audiovisual works standardized by [ISO 15706](https://www.iso.org/standard/83124.html). The ISAN remains persistent for a work regardless of its distribution format or its use. To facilitate human readability, the \"ISAN\" label, grouping hyphens, and two check characters are included (e.g., `ISAN 0000-0000-3A8D-0000-Z-0000-0000-6`); however, these elements shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `000000003A8D000000000000`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/provinceStateCode", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Text specifying a province or state.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
